title start
kind: plan
tags: plan
Plan page: a goal, the steps, and when it is done
title end

paragraph start
Use a plan page for work that has an end. It forces you to say what finished means, so the plan cannot be silently dropped.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Goal
title end

paragraph start
Write the outcome as one sentence, not an activity. Say what will be true when you are finished, for example a result someone could look at.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Steps
title end

paragraph start
Write each step as one action that can be finished and checked, one paragraph per step.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Put the steps in the order you will do them. If a step needs two actions, split it.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Done when
title end

paragraph start
Write the test that proves the goal is reached, so someone else could run it without asking you.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Open questions
title end

paragraph start
List what you do not know yet, and who can answer each question. Remove a question once it is answered.
paragraph end

section end

comment start
a goal, its steps, when it is done, what is open
comment end

